  "summary": "Ferrari, Cacciapuoti, Amoretti, and Caleffi analyze compiler design for distributed quantum computing, derive linear worst-case overhead bounds for remote-CNOT compilation strategies, implement a Qiskit-based compiler, and validate the bounds and strategy tradeoffs on medium-size quantum circuits.",
  "warnings": [
    "The source record date was null, but the source markdown front matter names January 22, 2021 as the date of publication.",
    "The markdown extraction is marked usable, but Table 1 numeric cells are not reliably preserved in the extracted text; evidence from the table is therefore represented qualitatively.",
    "Existing claim and relation files in the provided context refer to earlier compiler sources, so generated relations reference the newly extracted claims by index rather than existing canonical claim IDs."
